      "rev_n_2_3d7cb7_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_3d7cb7_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_3d7cb7",
        "thought_text": "The error in the code is due to an incorrect loop condition and the return statement being outside the function. The loop should iterate until `right < N` instead of `right <= N`, and the return statement should be inside the function. This will ensure that the function correctly processes the entire array and returns the length of the longest sub-array where each element appears exactly twice.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_3d7cb7_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2bdeef5f03",
        "created_at": 1794534062.5082543
      },
      "rev_n_3_ec95e4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ec95e4_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_ec95e4",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using a set to track unique elements, consider using a dictionary to count occurrences of each element in the current window. This approach allows for more efficient checking of the condition that each element appears exactly twice.",
